      {
        "id": 201384,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-01T08:59:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hmm, \"pareoidia\" doesn't seem to be a word - did you mean \"paranoia\"? If so, sure, that feeling that <em>something</em> is waiting to pounce on you, without you necssarily knowing what it is, could totally be something Sharp Fangs might embody (though I think Shadow probably embodies it the most). I feel more like a spirit of beasts would shape the <em>beasts</em>, however, to allow them to hide better among the plants, rather than reshaping the <em>plants</em> - that's what the plant spirits are for ;).</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:52.743Z",
