      {
        "id": 201387,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-02T16:41:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think they meant “pareidolia”, the tendency to see faces and other objects in random patterns. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes, I meant that one! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>One argument for why such a tendency would evolve is to help creatures identify possible predators lurking in hiding. Sounds a lot like Sharp Fangs to me!</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:29:52.947Z",
